{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T12:24:26-07:00","id":1098185,"title":"","content":"I imagine Changeling wars looking like two rival larp groups duking it out, to the general public. Maybe there will even be some normal dudes, joining the &quot;fun&quot; not knowing what's actually happening.<br /> <br /> Just don't think about supernatural wars the same way as for example WWI (what's the english word for 'Materialschlacht'?). Every life counts. The most effective weapon would be the one, that strikes by itself. Mobilizing a mob of normal humans against your enemy (in a kind of uproar against the government/banks/etc), blocking the enemies supplies, that's the tactics you'd use to hurt your rival factions.<br /> <br /> ___<br /> <br /> From my perspective there are 2 possibilities on how to run war scenarios. It depends a lot on what position the player characters have in the war. If they are the ones leading the war from a leaders or a strong position, it would be a lot about planning on how to secure points or objects of interest, luring out your enemies to crush them. It's more about strategy, intrigues and managing your resources aka your allies. Examples would be the Paradox Title Tyranny or Code Geass. The other position would be to be in the field, as a footsoldier or whatever fancy titles the characters have acquired. (Of course the general/leader aren't expelled from this type of event either) This would be a lot like a tactical RPG, an example would be the Commandos series, where you have to gather intel about your enemy and the pcs work together, make a plan etc. to win against the enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}